A version under history/ numbered major whose schema is backward compatible
with the one before it: cut numbers a version by the compatibility check, so
it was not cut so, and the diagnostic is an immutability violation naming
both files.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a:  string
	b?: int
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	a:  string
	b?: int
}
-- out/error --
error[E0207]: immutability violation: history/1.0.thema is backward compatible with history/0.0.thema
 --> history/1.0.thema:1:1
  |
1 | Schema: {
  | ^^^^^^
  |
 ::: history/0.0.thema:1:1
  |
1 | Schema: {
  | ------ the version before it
  |
  = note: a version that accepts all data the one before it accepts is a minor version, and 1.0 is a major version
  = help: run thema lineage check --published to find which file changed since it was cut, restore it, and make the change in tip.thema
